rding B1 might help One Voided Suit if we later discard all B tiles. So I think discard B1 is best.\n\nReason: Discarding B1 removes a terminal, making All Simples possible, and it is relatively safe based on opponents' melds and discards. Keeping T7 triplet maintains a pung for potential points, and keeping other B tiles might be discarded later to achieve One Voided Suit. The hand currently lacks a pair, so we need to draw a pair or convert a triplet into a pair later. Discarding B1 keeps flexibility.\n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
